{%- comment -%}
  This section uses Shopify's native Recommendations API with a server-side
  fallback, rather than a fully custom category-based renderer: the API's
  suggestions improve as order data accumulates, even though on a new store
  it may still return generic storewide lists at first. Only the
  locale-fallback heading logic below is custom.

  ONE cross-sell block, nothing else (no second rec feed).

  Mechanism: the section renders a server-side fallback from the product's
  first collection, and theme.js re-fetches this same section through the
  Recommendations API (?section_id=…&intent=related) and swaps in [data-related-grid]
  when the engine actually returns products — new stores often return none, which is
  why the collection fallback exists at all. Both paths use the stage-2 product card,
  so this row can never drift from the PLP.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%} This section uses an OFFER heading —
"Combine and receive an extra N% discount" — instead of a neutral "you may also like",
because that turns a related row into a reason to add a second piece.

Two things make it honest rather than a promise the checkout breaks:

  1. It renders ONLY while settings.qty_tiers_enabled is on, i.e. only once the matching
     Shopify automatic discounts actually exist. Off, the row falls back to the plain
     heading setting — so the offer wording is never live while no discount is.
  2. The percentage is READ FROM settings.qty_tiers, not typed in. A hardcoded
     percentage can silently disagree with the real ladder (e.g. copy says 15% while
     the ladder is 2:10, 3:15, 4:20). It now shows the top tier, which is the
     one worth advertising, and it can never drift from the ladder again. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign rel_heading = section.settings.heading
  assign rel_offer_tpl = section.settings.offer_heading
  unless request.locale.primary
    assign rel_heading = 'product.related.heading' | t
    assign rel_offer_tpl = 'product.related.offer_heading' | t
  endunless
  if settings.qty_tiers_enabled and settings.qty_tiers != blank
    assign rel_top_pct = 0
    assign rel_tiers = settings.qty_tiers | remove: ' ' | split: ','
    for rel_t in rel_tiers
      assign rel_parts = rel_t | split: ':'
      assign rel_p = rel_parts[1] | plus: 0
      if rel_p > rel_top_pct
        assign rel_top_pct = rel_p
      endif
    endfor
    if rel_top_pct > 0
      capture rel_heading
        echo rel_offer_tpl | default: 'Add another piece — save up to [pct]%' | replace: '[pct]', rel_top_pct
      endcapture
    endif
  endif
-%}
<section class="sec--tight related" data-related data-section-id="{{ section.id }}" data-product-id="{{ product.id }}" aria-label="{{ rel_heading | escape }}">
  <div class="wrap sec-head sec-head--center">
    <h2 class="dl">{{ rel_heading | escape }}</h2>
  </div>
  {%- if recommendations.performed and recommendations.products_count > 0 -%}
    <div class="grid-4" data-related-grid data-related-target>
      {%- for p in recommendations.products limit: 6 -%}
        {% render 'product-card', product: p, card_index: forloop.index %}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign rel_col = product.collections.first -%}
    {%- assign shown = 0 -%}
    {%- if rel_col and rel_col.products.size > 1 -%}
      <div class="grid-4 product-grid" data-related-target>
        {%- for p in rel_col.products limit: 12 -%}
          {%- unless p.id == product.id or shown >= 6 -%}
            {%- assign shown = shown | plus: 1 -%}
            {% render 'product-card', product: p, card_index: shown %}
          {%- endunless -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment -%} nothing to show yet: theme.js removes the whole section when the
      API comes back empty too, so no skeleton is ever left stranded {%- endcomment -%}
      <div data-related-target hidden></div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "PDP related products",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "You may also like", "info": "Shown while the bundle discounts are switched off." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "offer_heading", "label": "Offer heading (bundle discounts on)", "default": "Add another piece — save up to [pct]%", "info": "Replaces the heading above once Bundle discounts are enabled. [pct] is filled in with the highest tier from the ladder, so the number can never disagree with the offer." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "PDP related products" }]
}
{% endschema %}
